[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Still/images/banner.jpg?v=2[/img]

Home brewing and distilling for [b]Build 42[/b]. Mash, ferment, distil, make the cuts, age it in oak, or run a generator on it.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Yes. The server decides every batch[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedStill[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Still/images/h-mash.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Still/images/mash.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Learn the recipes from [i]The Home Brewer[/i], a magazine found in kitchens, bars, barns and on magazine racks, or level up Cooking (4 to 6, by recipe).
[*]In a bucket with 8 L of water: grain and hops make wort, grain alone makes a grain mash, potatoes and a little grain make a potato mash, sugar makes a sugar mash and honey makes a honey must.
[*]Press 12 apples or grapes into juice. Vanilla juices ferment too.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Still/images/h-ferment.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Still/images/ferment.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Make a [b]Fermenting Bucket[/b] from a bucket and an airlock (a cork or jar lid and a rubber band), or throw a [b]Stoneware Crock[/b] on a pottery wheel and fire it in a kiln. Crocks also turn up as loot.
[*]Pour the mash in with the game's own fluid menu, right-click the fermenter and pitch yeast: a yeast packet, a yeast starter, or wild yeast for fruit and honey.
[*]Wort becomes beer in about 4 days, apple juice cider in 7, grape and other juices wine in 10, honey must mead in 14. Grain, potato and sugar mashes become a wash for the still.
[*]18-24 °C is ideal. Cold slows it and near freezing stops it; heat speeds it up but risks souring the batch. With Dazed Climate the fermenter reads its room's temperature.
[*]A crock holds 40 L, keeps its temperature steadier and sours less than a 20 L bucket.
[*]Save the yeast sediment in a jar for a starter. Feed it flour or sugar every two weeks to keep it alive.
[*]A hydrometer shows the exact progress and time left.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Still/images/h-distil.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Still/images/distil.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Three stills from [i]Mountain Spirits[/i]: a [b]Makeshift Still[/b] from a pot and a bucket (8 L, wood or electric), a [b]Salvaged Still[/b] welded from a steel tank or sheet metal (40 L, propane or electric), and the two-square [b]Copper Pot Still[/b] (60 L, wood, with a thumper).
[*]Pour in a wash, wine or beer, add fuel, fill the cooling tub and light it. Grain makes moonshine, sugar makes raw rum, wine and cider make raw brandy. Run spirit again for 90% high-proof.
[*]Make the cuts yourself on the still panel: foreshots, heads, hearts, tails. Walk away and your Cooking skill makes them. Foreshots are poison and a bad cut gives Bad Moonshine.
[*]A still that boils its cooling tub dry can catch fire, and the copper still's thumper draws zombies.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Still/images/h-age.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Still/images/age.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Char an [b]Oak Ageing Barrel[/b] and fill it: moonshine and raw brandy become Whiskey and Brandy in 90 days, raw rum becomes Rum in 60.
[*]Proof high-proof down to Vodka, or add a splash of petrol to make fuel ethanol.
[*]Generators take an ethanol blend up to 15%, or any blend with an [b]Ethanol Carburettor Kit[/b].
[/list]

[h2]With other Dazed mods[/h2]
Essentials cleans bandages with moonshine. Plumbing pipes water to the cooling tub and propane to the salvaged still. Power counts an electric still as a load. Salvage and Butchery parts fit the recipes. Climate sets the fermenting temperature.

[h2]Sandbox[/h2]
Fermenting, distilling and ageing speed, souring chance, wild yeast, poison from bad cuts, still fires, thumper noise, the ethanol blend limit, all recipes known, and how much loot spawns. Dazed Core's presets set them.

